      "problem": "$\\sqrt{2}≈1.414$ can be expressed as",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the given approximation can be written using exponents as follows:\n\n$$\n{2}^{1/2}≈1.412\n$$\n\nThe logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a={b}^{x}$ is equivalent to ${log}_{b}⁡a=x$\n\nIf we compare ${2}^{1/2}≈1.412$ with $a={b}^{x},$ we get $a=1.412,b=2$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the approximation $\\sqrt{2}≈1.414$ can be expressed as ${log}_{2}⁡(1.414)≈\\frac{1}{2}.$",
